{"schema_version":1,"search_id":"09595fb8c42c4d37848886e8cb55aabe","seq":62,"turn":2,"at_ms":13504.7232920042,"type":"search_finished","result":{"question":{"content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Did last month's latency spike come from the new reranker, and is it fixed?"}]},"hits":[{"hit":{"doc_id":"DEP-0913-07","source":"deploys","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api v4.12\n\nRolled out search-api v4.12 to production (canary 10% at 16:05, full at 17:30 UTC). Changes: cross-encoder ranking now serves all search traffic, reranker v2 flag default on (PR 1187); bumps the protobuf library; drops the unused legacy facets endpoint. Canary checks passed on error rate. Rollback plan: previous image v4.11.3."}],"metadata":{"date":"2026-09-13","service":"search-api","version":"4.12","pr":1187,"author":"Marcus Chen","title":"search-api v4.12"},"raw_score":null,"provenance":[{"turn":1,"call_id":"t1.c2","rank":0}]},"score":0.925597,"p_relevant":1.0,"rationale":"Shows the reranker v2 was deployed in search-api v4.12, causing the spike.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"PR-1203","source":"pull_requests","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Smaller inference batches and a candidate embedding cache for ranking\n\nFixes INC-4821, a regression from PR 1187. Reranker v2 with batch size 64 queued requests behind each other under peak load, which pushed tail latency up. This PR rolls the batch size back to 16 and adds an LRU cache for candidate embeddings so repeat queries skip the encoder. Load test: p95 back to 175 ms at 2x peak traffic. Deployed with search-api v4.12.2."}],"metadata":{"number":1203,"merged":"2026-09-18","service":"search-api","author":"Marcus Chen","title":"Smaller inference batches and a candidate embedding cache for ranking"},"raw_score":null,"provenance":[{"turn":1,"call_id":"t1.c3","rank":1}]},"score":0.925184,"p_relevant":1.0,"rationale":"Confirms reranker v2 caused latency (INC-4821) and explains the fix in PR-1203.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"DEP-0918-05","source":"deploys","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api v4.12.2\n\nRolled out search-api v4.12.2 (PR 1203). Canary at 13:10 UTC, full at 14:25 UTC."}],"metadata":{"date":"2026-09-18","service":"search-api","version":"4.12.2","pr":1203,"author":"Marcus Chen","title":"search-api v4.12.2"},"raw_score":null,"provenance":[{"turn":1,"call_id":"t1.c2","rank":4}]},"score":0.924022,"p_relevant":1.0,"rationale":"Mentions deployment of v4.12.2 which addresses the latency issue.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4821","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api p95 elevated across all regions\n\nOpened by on-call (Priya Raman) at 09:12 UTC after the SLO burn alert fired. search-api p95 latency climbed from ~180 ms to ~640 ms starting early Sept 14 and is holding there. p50 is only slightly up. Error rate is flat, so requests succeed but slowly. CPU on the search-api pods is up ~35%. Checked the CDN and the edge cache: both look normal. No config pushes in the last 12 hours. Mitigation so far: scaled search-api from 24 to 36 pods, which took p95 down to ~520 ms but did not clear it. Root cause: not yet identified. Leaving open for the search team to investigate on Monday. Customer impact: slower search results pages, some timeouts on the mobile app's type-ahead."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-09-14","service":"search-api","severity":"SEV2","status":"resolved","title":"search-api p95 elevated across all regions"},"raw_score":0.6489217206265213,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c0","rank":4},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c3","rank":2},{"turn":1,"call_id":"t1.c0","rank":0},{"turn":2,"call_id":"t2.c2","rank":0}]},"score":0.91,"p_relevant":0.9,"rationale":"Search-api latency spike in September.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"DASH-W38-search","source":"dashboards","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api weekly SLO report, week 38\n\nWeek of Sept 14–20. p95 was 610 ms Monday to Thursday morning, above the 300 ms SLO; from Sept 18 afternoon p95 dropped to 176 ms and stayed at baseline through Sunday. p50 98 ms for the week. Availability 99.95%. Error budget: 38% used this week."}],"metadata":{"service":"search-api","week":"2026-W38","week_start":"2026-09-14","week_end":"2026-09-20","title":"search-api weekly SLO report, week 38"},"raw_score":0.7706531286239624,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c4","rank":4},{"turn":1,"call_id":"t1.c1","rank":0},{"turn":2,"call_id":"t2.c0","rank":1}]},"score":0.884803,"p_relevant":0.9,"rationale":"Search weekly report for the period covering the September latency spike and resolution.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"PR-1165","source":"pull_requests","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Reranker v2 experiment at 5%\n\nRaises the reranker v2 experiment from 1% to 5%. Experiment p95 latency +9 ms at 5%."}],"metadata":{"number":1165,"merged":"2026-08-31","service":"search-api","author":"Marcus Chen","title":"Reranker v2 experiment at 5%"},"raw_score":0.986053408104363,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":3},{"turn":1,"call_id":"t1.c4","rank":3}]},"score":0.318794,"p_relevant":0.3,"rationale":"Mentions reranker latency impact.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"PR-1187","source":"pull_requests","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Roll out reranker v2 to all search traffic\n\nThis turns on reranker v2 (the cross-encoder model) for 100% of search requests, up from the 5% experiment. Offline NDCG@10 is +4.1% over v1. Batch size is set to 64 to keep GPU utilisation high. Rollout is behind the reranker_v2 flag so we can turn it off. Reviewers: @lortiz @pramam."}],"metadata":{"number":1187,"merged":"2026-09-12","service":"search-api","author":"Marcus Chen","title":"Roll out reranker v2 to all search traffic"},"raw_score":0.6295955411460765,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":7},{"turn":1,"call_id":"t1.c3","rank":0},{"turn":1,"call_id":"t1.c4","rank":7}]},"score":0.251521,"p_relevant":0.2,"rationale":"Reranker v2 rollout.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"PR-1215